            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0150" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 a 1/369</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Coolidge to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rapid City, S. Dak.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 5.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have your letter of the
                    28th, with the enclosure from the British Ambassador, both of which I have read
                    with care. Your position seems to me correct and satisfactory.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Calvin Coolidge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
